package cli

var usage = "soho — role-agent layer over the `herdr` CLI.\n\nRoles are markdown files with frontmatter (roles/<role>.md, overridable per\nproject in .agents/soho-roles/<role>.md). The native command spawns one CLI agent\nper role in a Herdr pane, dispatches a composed prompt (role body + brief),\nand detects completion through a file-based report contract. Only the `job` supervisor pushes the job branch and opens a draft pull request;\nnothing else commits or pushes, and nothing closes panes it did not\ncreate.\n\nUsage:\n  soho inventory --json              # read-only local agent inventory\n  soho init                          # doctor + name the caller `orchestrator`, print context\n  soho title \"<objective>\" | title --clear   # this pane's title: orchestrator: <objective>\n  soho doctor [--fix] [--panes 2|3|4] [--user|--session]\n                                             # advisory check; --fix normalizes lanes in the project file\n  soho explain                       # plain text for a person: what is running, or how to start\n  soho setup [--local | --target FILE] [--no-hooks] [--guard-hooks] [--dry-run]\n                     [--detect | --probe [--kind K --model M] [--timeout S]\n                      | --plan [--panes 2|3|4] [--lane name=kind[:model[:effort]]]\n                        [--set K V] [--user-set K V] [--session-set K V]]\n                     [--panes 2|3|4] [--lane name=kind[:model[:effort]]]\n                                             # write the block + hooks; --local uses CLAUDE.local.md and Git info/exclude; --detect/--probe/--plan print and write nothing\n  soho setup --roles [--plan | --dry-run]   # move .agents/herdr-roles/ to .agents/soho-roles/ only (and its Git info/exclude line); no block, no hooks\n  soho hook reminder|doctor|inbound  # native agent hooks, silent outside Herdr; reminder and inbound check the peer messages of a Claude Code prompt first (the project's inbound=off refuses with exit 18; a prompt over 4 MiB is blocked)\n  soho install [--version vTAG] [--dir PATH]\n                                             # portable installer: downloads the release binary for this platform, verifies it against SHA256SUMS, installs it to --dir (default $SOHO_INSTALL_DIR, or $HOME/.local/bin on POSIX / %LOCALAPPDATA%/Programs/soho on Windows); prints the installed path, digest and PATH advice (no automatic shell or registry edits); without --version it resolves the newest release of the running binary's channel (rc for a pre-release build, stable otherwise) and refuses a tag lower than the running version (exit 2; pass --version to install it)\n  soho update --check [--json] [--channel stable|rc]\n       soho update [--channel stable|rc]\n       soho update --version vTAG\n                                             # --check answers without installing (one text line, or one --json object; exit 0 when checked, 1 when it could not check), and its advice names --channel when that differs from the binary's own; the other forms install the newest release of the running binary's channel (rc for a pre-release build, stable otherwise; --channel overrides it) or exactly vTAG, SHA256SUMS verified, into the directory of the running executable, whose name must be the canonical one (a renamed binary is refused with exit 2); a channel release lower than the running version is refused without --version; after installing it prints the soho setup --local next step and, when ~/.agents/skills/soho exists, the npx -y skills add \"djalmajr/soho#<tag>\" --global --skill soho -y command (printed, never run); doctor and init print one passive `update available: <tag> (soho update)` line, cached 24 h in the state dir (update_check=off or SOHO_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1 turns it off)\n  soho roles [--json] | kinds\n  soho config [set <key> <value> [--project|--user] [--dry-run [--json]] | get <key> | unset <key> [--project|--user]]\n                                             # set writes the project file (.agents/soho.conf) unless --user; --dry-run prints the plan and writes nothing (--json adds the preview); unset removes one key; for this session only, use soho session set\n  soho session [set <key> <value> | clear [key] | show]\n                                             # this-session overrides in <state>/session.conf\n  soho models <kind>                 # ids the CLI lists, newest first\n  soho model <kind> <spec> [effort]  # how a model spec resolves\n  soho regrid                        # exact grids: caller tab (layout=split) + every herd tab\n  soho promote                       # promote this calling sub-orchestrator to orchestrator\n                                             # keeps its pane; refuses unresolved tasks, active collaborations and owned live resources\n  soho tab-label [<text>] [--tab ID] [--auto]\n                                             # list herd tabs / pin a tab's label / back to automatic\n  soho layout-plan [--layout FILE] [--me P] [--mine \"P…\"]\n                                             # where the next split-layout spawn would go, and why\n  soho role <name>\n  soho help [<command>]              # this text, or the lines of one command (as <command> --help)\n  soho spawn <role> [--name N] [--kind K] [--direction right|down]\n                      [--ratio F] [--cwd DIR] [--pane ID] [--timeout MS]\n                      [--effort low|medium|high|xhigh|max] [--model M]\n                      [--approvals ask|edits|auto|full|unsandboxed] [--mcp inherit|none|a,b] [--reuse|--fresh]\n                      [--env-from NAME]... [--tab-label TEXT] [--force] [-- <native agent args>]\n    --env-from NAME  Copy an explicit executor variable to a fresh native HC Pi child (repeatable; maximum 16 distinct names). Spawn backend diagnostics and printed spawn metadata replace exact handed-off values with [redacted:NAME] (minimum 4 bytes). Split, URL-encoded and base64 forms are not protected. Core admission and pressure warnings are not filtered, and the terminal address is stored in the roster as the backend returned it. Core retains overrides; this is not a vault; forward NONSECRET metadata, never API keys.\n  soho env                          # environment block for a feedback issue\n  soho lint <brief.md> [--role <role>]  # check the dispatch brief diagnostics without dispatching\n  soho validate [--layer <name>]... [--timeout MS] [--plan] [--json]\n                                             # run VALIDATION.md's test layers in file order (sh -c at the project root; 30m per layer by default, never stopping at a failure) and report one result per layer plus the worst overall; --plan runs nothing; evidence under <state>/validation/<stamp>/; exits 0 PASS, 1 FAIL, 5 BLOCKED or NOT RUN\n  soho send <ref|name> <message…> | --file <path> [--now] [--timeout MS]\n                      [--assignment ID --type review.question]\n                                             # peer message to an agent of any kind (a reference, or a name on the local server); waits for a busy target to settle by default; the target project's inbound=off refuses (exit 18)\n  soho dispatch <agent> <brief.md> [--role R] [--timeout MS]\n                      [--no-wait] [--amend]\n                      [--compact] [--resend] [--queue] [--when-idle] [--allow-full-context]\n                                             # --amend sends <file> as an amendment to the agent's current brief, with a new report that wait watches\n                                             # --allow-full-context bypasses context_fresh_percent refusal for pi/opencode; the context warning still prints\n                                             # --compact compacts an idle worker (claude, codex, pi) before the brief; a timeout or a busy worker exits 9/10 and the brief is not sent\n                                             # --resend sends the brief again when the same brief of the task is already open; the default sends nothing and waits on the task's current report (duplicate_of in the JSON)\n                                             # --queue types the brief now to a worker that is still working or blocked on its open task (today's queued behavior); without it the dispatch refuses (exit 10) until the report exists\n  soho compact <agent> [--timeout MS]\n                                             # send /compact once to an idle worker and wait for the CLI's proof plus its return to idle; a kind without a verified command exits 2, a timeout 9 (status timeout JSON)\n  soho model-set <worker> <provider/model> [--effort <level>] [--interrupt]\n                                             # type /model (and /thinking) into a live pi worker through its own terminal, verify the footer, then record the model and effort in the roster; a non-pi worker exits 2, a draft exits 10, an unverified footer exits 1\n  soho wait <agent>... [--timeout MS] [--any] [--wake | --observe]\n                                             # --wake (native Core, SOHO_TRANSPORT=hc, only) starts one child terminal of the caller that runs a non-settling wait and exits when the agents settle, so its exit note wakes an orchestrator whose turn has ended; prints one JSON line (wake armed, or already-armed when that child is live) and exits 0; the orchestrator then runs a plain soho wait <agent>, which settles at once with every field; on the legacy TUI it exits 2\n                                             # a plain --wake first stops this caller's own previous recorded wakes (kill then rm through the transport) and arms exactly the given agents; the arming line lists the stopped addresses in replaced. --add keeps the older behavior: skip agents covered by a live wake of this caller and answer already-armed when none are left. A killed observer prints one interrupted line with the command to rearm.\n                                             # --observe is the probe that child runs (not for direct use): the same loop, exit codes and statuses as a plain wait, but a done report is left unsettled (no task state, metrics, warnings, mirror or git audit) and the line carries the key observe (true)\n  soho status [<agent>...]           # no names = the whole team; gone = agent_not_found; not-in-roster = known to Herdr, not this workspace's team; unavailable = agent get failed (exit 4)\n  soho collect <agent> [--lines N] [--verify]\n                                             # --verify checks the sha256 lines of the last report (exit 16 on changed/missing, or when no sha256 line is found)\n  soho stats [--since <date|50m|12h|1d|2w>] [--by role|kind|model|kind-model|agent|effort|author-model|type|origin|class] [--json]  # tasks, times and review findings; --by groups results\n  soho metrics mark <report> [--finding <n>=real|false]... [--missed P0|P1|P2|P3]... [--amendment implementer|brief]\n                                             # label a report after checking it (its metrics line was recorded with metrics=on)\n  soho metrics export [--since <date|50m|12h|1d|2w>] [--project-label <label>]\n                                             # anonymized summary of metrics.jsonl, one JSON line per report\n  soho metrics table [--write <file>] <export.jsonl>...\n                                             # markdown table per role, slice type and model from exported summaries; --write replaces the generated block of <file>\n  soho run <role> <brief.md> [spawn/dispatch options] [-- <agent args>]\n  soho collaborate start <author> <reviewer> --brief <path> [--max-rounds N]\n                      | status <assignment> [--json]\n                      | event <assignment> ready|findings|corrected|approved|escalate --report <path> --revision <fingerprint>\n                      | stop <assignment>\n                      | finalize <assignment> --verdict accept|reject\n                                             # optional worker_messages=policy; assigned local pair; orchestrator creates/finalizes; typed events bind the reviewed revision\n  soho job start --id <id> --repo <org/repo> [--base <branch>] [--mode worktree|workspace]\n                       [--brief <file|->] [--timeout <minutes>] [--dry-run]\n  soho job status --id <id>\n  soho job wait --id <id> [--timeout MS]\n  soho job events --id <id> [--since <seq>] [--wait MS]\n  soho job collect --id <id> [--md] [--verify]\n  soho job amend --id <id> [<file>|-]\n  soho job send --id <id> [<file>|-]\n  soho job ack --id <id> --upto <seq>\n  soho job cancel --id <id> [--grace <seconds>]\n  soho job close --id <id> [--force]\n  soho job list [--state <state>]\n  soho job supervise --id <id> [--repo <org/repo>]\n  soho job checkpoint --id <id>\n  soho job note --id <id> --tipo <type> [--escopo global|projeto] [--motivo <text>] [--refs k=v,...] [<summary>|-]\n  soho capabilities --json            # shared engine capability schema\n  soho report <agent> | --file <path> [--json]\n                                             # read-only parsed report: items, counts, test layers, review responses and wait warnings\n  soho roster [--scope workspace|server] [--json]\n  soho find [words] [--machine <label>]... [--all] [--json] [--timeout MS]\n                                             # live panes with a paste-ready session reference ([machine/]<pane id>)\n  soho release <agent> [--close] [--force] [--keep-copies] [--keep-procs]\n                                             # --keep-copies leaves the agent's registered copies for gc instead of removing them\n                                             # --keep-procs leaves the agent's registered processes for gc instead of stopping them\n  soho reopen <agent> [--force] [--kind K] [--model M] [--effort low|medium|high|xhigh|max] [--redispatch]\n                                             # release --close + spawn --fresh with the role, kind, model, effort, cwd and native args (overrides replace the roster's kind/model/effort; --kind without --model lets the kind resolve its own model); output: the spawn JSON, then the dispatch JSON with --redispatch\n  soho clean [--older-than DAYS]\n  soho copies\n                                             # list the copy registry: <path>  <owner>  <age>  <state> (owned | orphan | missing); read-only\n  soho copies add <path> [--agent <name>]\n                                             # register a copy made by hand (origin add); a path that fails the safety check or is not an existing directory refuses (exit 2), an unknown --agent exits 3\n  soho copies release <path>...\n                                             # owner removes registered copies\n  soho procs\n                                             # list the process registry: <pid>  <name>  <owner>  <age>  <state> (running | gone | reused); read-only\n  soho procs add <pid> [--agent <name>]\n                                             # register a worker process (its start time and command name; the command line is never read); a pid that is not a positive integer, pid 1, this process, its parent, or not running refuses (exit 2), an unknown --agent exits 3\n  soho procs stop <pid>… [--agent <name>]\n                                             # stop only the calling agent's registered processes; --agent must match a roster-mapped calling pane; exits 0 stopped/already gone, 2 usage/refusal, 4 stop failed; all pids are processed and the worst code wins\n  soho gc [--yes] [--verbose] [--older-than HOURS] [--include-unregistered]\n                                             # dry run lists orphan copies at least HOURS old (default 2) plus unregistered mutation copies; --verbose lists other projects individually; --yes removes them (unregistered only with --include-unregistered)\n  soho friction [--since D|50m|12h|1d|2w] [--level L] [--command C] [--agent A] [--summary | --patterns [--json]]  # errors/warnings of this workspace; options AND together; --patterns groups the lines by their masked message template (count, after, key, last_seen, fixed_by, pattern) and --json returns the same as JSON\n  soho friction add \"<text>\" [--brief <path>] [--key <slug>]  # record one friction note (level note, command friction; --key writes it as '[<slug>] <text>', the key of the pattern it belongs to)\n  soho friction fixed <key> \"<what resolved it>\"  # mark a friction pattern fixed (level fixed, command friction); the key must exist in the log; a second fixed replaces fixed_by and restarts the after count without erasing the first\n  soho feedback send <report.md> \"<one-line summary>\"\n                                             # feedback=local: file the report in feedback_dir; one line to feedback_to when set\n  soho resume [<agent>…] [--all] [--dry-run]\n  soho review-snapshot <worktree> [--for <agent>] [--name <slug>] [--base <rev>]\n                                             # An existing file or link at either artifact name is refused with exit 2; the existing entry and any link target remain untouched.\n  soho mutation-guard <copy-dir> [--source <dir>] [--env NAME]...\n  soho mutation-copy [--source <dir>] [--dest <dir>] [--print-path] [--exclude <glob>]... [--link <relpath>=<target>]...\n  soho gate <prefix> <duration> -- <program> [args…]\n                                             # run one program directly (no shell) under a bound of 1s to 1h and record <prefix>.command.json (argv, cwd, bound, started; never the environment), <prefix>.stdout, <prefix>.stderr and <prefix>.result.json (pid, native_exit, signal, context_expired, wait_joined, wait_error, start_error), all mode 0600; an existing artifact or a missing parent directory refuses (exit 2) before anything starts; on expiry it terminates the started process and its process group, waits 5 seconds, then kills (Windows: the direct child only); needs no Herdr context; prints pid=<pid> native_exit=<n> context_expired=<bool> wait_joined=<bool>; exits with the program's code, 124 when the bound expired, 125 when it could not start or was killed by a signal, 2 on usage\n\nDurations: --timeout (and job events --wait) takes milliseconds, or a number with ms, s, m or h (90s, 30m, 2h).\n\nCompletion contract: without an assignment, a worker finishes when its report exists.\nAn active collaboration has phase/round/revision/delivery; only orchestrator finalize\nends it. Reports remain round evidence, and release refuses active participants. Use\n`dispatch` (waits by default), `wait` (one or many agents), or `status`\n(non-blocking). Never poll `herdr agent get` state alone: integrations\nreport idle/done mid-task.\n\nConfiguration (key=value files; later layers win, env wins over files,\nflags win over env):\n  model_cap=<n>|off       live workers per model (off = no cap); a lane with\n                          lane.<name>.models=m1,m2 picks the first model below the cap at spawn\n  <skill>/config.defaults → ~/.config/soho/config\n  → <repo>/.agents/soho.conf → <state>/session.conf (session)\n  → SOHO_<KEY> → flags\n\nExit codes: 2 usage/env · 3 unknown role/agent · 4 local state or Git ignore I/O failure, or Herdr failure (includes\n`herdr agent get` transport/permission errors reported as `unavailable`) ·\n6 settled without report or agent really gone ·\n7 agent blocked (startup or approval) or asked a question · 8 max_workers reached ·\n9 wait timeout · 10 lane busy · 11 quota exhausted · 12 planner is the orchestrator ·\n13 lane kind-mismatch (set lane.<name>.kind, or release the lane) or every model of a lane's models list at model_cap ·\n14 provider error or capacity · 15 prompt not received, or send not\ntaken (lost / unverified) ·\n16 collect --verify: a reported file changed or is missing, or nothing was verified ·\n17 send: the target is still busy after the wait timeout, or shows a\ndialog; nothing was sent ·\n18 send: the target project refuses peer messages (inbound=off), or its hook refused this one (refused-…) ·\n19 job failed · 20 job id reused with another brief · 21 job canceled ·\n22 job preparation failed · 24 job close with unacknowledged decisions ·\n25 spawn refused under resource pressure.\n"
